The legal text is the Constitution of the State of Iowa (codified) and chapters of the Iowa Code (2026 edition), as published by the
Iowa Legislative Services Agency on www.legis.iowa.gov. The Legislature designates its electronic editions as official legal
material under Iowa Code chapter 2B (the Uniform Electronic Legal Material Act). Its disclaimer page restricts only photographs and
video captions, and states no copyright claim over the text of the Code or the Constitution.

Statutes and constitutions are works of government that carry no copyright (Georgia v. Public.Resource.Org, Inc., 590 U.S. ___, 2020).
Only the text of each section and its source note is taken; the Legislature's footnotes are left out.

The arrangement of this repository, its tables, commit messages and tools are by Lexifina and may be reused under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). This repository is not legal advice
and not an official publication. Source: Iowa Legislative Services Agency, www.legis.iowa.gov.
